      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/leon_virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The post office adopted the name Leon in 1841, a change whose origin remains unclear but cemented the town’s identity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/leon_virginia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Leon sits along the Kanawha River, a waterway that cuts through the entire state of West Virginia.",
